## The front-door weblog's static pages ("About this site"), in the front
## door's own chrome. Without a _page of its own this theme fell through to
## the shared templates/weblog/page.vm, whose body carries no fd class -- a
## browser-default page inside an otherwise designed site.
##
## Built from _header/_footer like the other two views, so the head (CSP,
## SEO, analytics, every asset macro) stays in one place. The page's own
## title is the h1 here, so the header steps the site name down to a
## paragraph ($fdReading). $model.page.title is stored RAW (PageBean.copyTo),
## so it is escaped below and by the header; a meta title is the whole tab
## title, as on every theme.
#set($fdPageTitle = $model.page.title)
#set($fdMetaTitle = $model.page.metaTitle)
#set($fdReading = true)
#includeTemplate($model.weblog "_header")

## pressroom-content puts the article inside the content assets' scope
## (callouts, code blocks, heading anchors), as the shared fallback did.
<article class="fd-page pressroom-content">
    <h1 class="fd-page-title">$utils.escapeHTML($model.page.title)</h1>
    <div class="fd-prose">$model.page.renderedContent</div>
</article>

#includeTemplate($model.weblog "_footer")
